### 🟢 GPT-5 Web Search Example
# Endpoint: /gpt5
# Purpose: Sends a prompt to the GPT-5 model with web search enabled
#          Retrieves a real-time, AI-generated interesting fact about GPT-5.
# Usage: Simply send a GET request. No parameters are needed.
# Response: Plain text content returned by the AI model.
GET http://localhost:8080/gpt5
Accept: application/json


### 🟢 Spring Ecosystem News Aggregator
# Endpoint: /news
# Purpose: Retrieves curated, up-to-date news from the Spring ecosystem.
#          Collects information from official blogs, GitHub releases,
#          security updates, and major Spring announcements.
# Usage: Send a GET request. This endpoint automatically checks
#        the past 7 days and expands to the last month if needed.
# Response: Plain text summary with date, source, impact level,
#           brief summary, and developer action items.
GET http://localhost:8080/news
Accept: application/json


### 🟢 Restaurant Finder (Default Parameters)
# Endpoint: /restaurants
# Purpose: Provides exactly 3 restaurant recommendations near default location
#          (Cleveland, Ohio, US) using real-time web search.
#          Uses default cuisine: any, price range: $, timezone: America/New_York.
# Usage: Send a GET request. Optional query parameters exist if customization is needed
# Response: Plain text with exactly 3 restaurants, including:
#           - Restaurant Name & Neighborhood
#           - Specialty
#           - Price & Rating
#           - Status & Contact info
GET http://localhost:8080/restaurants
Accept: application/json
